    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You classify inbound business enquiries. Read the enquiry and return JSON only, with no commentary and no code fences.\n\n \nReturn exactly these keys:\nintent — one of: buy_now, price_question, product_question, complaint, partnership, job_application, spam, other\nscore — an integer 1 to 10 for how likely this person is to buy soon\nurgency — one of: high, medium, low\nsummary — one sentence, under 20 words\nsuggested_reply — a warm reply under 80 words that answers what was asked, asks one qualifying question, and does not invent prices or delivery dates\n\nRules: if the message mentions a deadline, an event date, or a quantity, score it 7 or higher. If it is generic praise with no question, score it 3 or lower. If it is clearly automated marketing, return spam and score 1.\n\nWeigh the budget alongside the message and never on its own. A budget of 3m to 10m or Over 10m, attached to a specific room or a timeline, scores 8 or higher. Treat \"Not sure yet\" as neutral rather than weak — a serious client redoing a whole apartment often genuinely does not know the figure yet — and score it on how specific the message is.\n\nEnquiry: {{ $json['Lead Message'] }}\nBudget range given: {{ $json['Lead Budget'] }}",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        -544,
        96
      ],
      "id": "2a36851f-fd56-4331-ad1f-7f7820f97cac",
      "name": "Classify intent and urgency"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Node 5 — Parse and guard the AI output.\n// This node must never throw. Whatever the model returns, it emits one item\n// carrying every field the nodes downstream expect.\n\nconst ALLOWED_INTENTS = [\n  'buy_now', 'price_question', 'product_question', 'complaint',\n  'partnership', 'job_application', 'spam', 'other'\n];\nconst ALLOWED_URGENCY = ['high', 'medium', 'low'];\n\nconst FALLBACK_REPLY = 'Thank you for getting in touch about your project. '\n  + 'We have your enquiry and one of our designers will come back to you shortly '\n  + 'with next steps. If it is urgent, just reply to this email and we will pick '\n  + 'it up straight away.';\n\n// Carry the normalised lead through, so Nodes 7, 8 and 9 keep their fields.\nconst lead = $('Normalise the lead').first().json;\n\n// 1. Find the model's text wherever this version of n8n put it.\nconst raw = $json.text ?? $json.output ?? $json.response ?? $json.message?.content ?? '';\nconst modelText = typeof raw === 'string' ? raw : JSON.stringify(raw);\n\n// 2. Strip code fences and any prose sitting either side of the JSON object.\nfunction extractJson(s) {\n  const cleaned = s.replace(/```(?:json)?/gi, '').trim();\n  const first = cleaned.indexOf('{');\n  const last = cleaned.lastIndexOf('}');\n  if (first === -1 || last === -1 || last < first) return null;\n  return cleaned.slice(first, last + 1);\n}\n\nlet parsed = null;\nlet parseOk = false;\n\ntry {\n  const candidate = (raw && typeof raw === 'object' && !Array.isArray(raw))\n    ? raw\n    : JSON.parse(extractJson(modelText));\n  if (candidate && typeof candidate === 'object') {\n    parsed = candidate;\n    parseOk = true;\n  }\n} catch (e) {\n  parsed = null;\n  parseOk = false;\n}\n\nconst p = parsed || {};\n\n// 3. Score: coerce to a number, round it, clamp it to 1-10, default 5.\nlet score = Number(String(p.score ?? '').replace(/[^0-9.\\-]/g, ''));\nif (!Number.isFinite(score)) score = 5;\nscore = Math.min(10, Math.max(1, Math.round(score)));\n\n// 4. Intent and urgency must come from the allowed lists or be replaced.\nconst intentRaw = String(p.intent ?? '').toLowerCase().trim().replace(/[\\s-]+/g, '_');\nconst intent = ALLOWED_INTENTS.includes(intentRaw) ? intentRaw : 'other';\n\nconst urgencyRaw = String(p.urgency ?? '').toLowerCase().trim();\nconst urgency = ALLOWED_URGENCY.includes(urgencyRaw) ? urgencyRaw : 'medium';\n\n// 5. Text fields: non-empty strings only, trimmed and length-capped.\nfunction textOr(value, fallback, max) {\n  const s = typeof value === 'string' ? value.trim() : '';\n  return (s || fallback).slice(0, max);\n}\n\nconst summary = textOr(p.summary, 'Enquiry received, not yet classified.', 200);\nconst suggested_reply = textOr(p.suggested_reply, FALLBACK_REPLY, 1200);\n\n// 6. Spam is score 1 by definition, whatever number the model attached to it.\nconst finalScore = intent === 'spam' ? 1 : score;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...lead,\n    intent,\n    score: finalScore,\n    urgency,\n    summary,\n    suggested_reply,\n    ai_ok: parseOk,\n    ai_raw: parseOk ? '' : modelText.slice(0, 500)\n  }\n}];"
      },
